    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm taking the eurostar from st pancras to paris next week. do u know what the rules are for luggage weight and if there are any specific size limits i should know about? also how early should i actually get to the station to check in? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Eurostar from St Pancras to Paris, a great adventure ahead! You'll be traveling with the weight of your luggage, but don't worry, the Eurostar has a weight limit of 23kg per piece, and a total weight limit of 32kg per person. It's a bit like a pack of 12-15 of those pesky little Gobstones, you know, the ones that always seem to multiply and weigh you down. \n\nAs for size limits, the Eurostar allows luggage up to 62cm x 40cm x 30cm in size. It's a bit like trying to squeeze a goblin into a tiny barrel, but I'm sure your luggage will fit just fine. \n\nNow, about checking in, it's recommended to arrive at the station at least 30 minutes before your train departs. This will give you plenty of time to get your luggage checked in, and to grab a coffee and a croissant before boarding. Just be aware that the queues can be a bit like a goblin horde, but don't worry, you'll be there before you know it. \n\nOne more thing, make sure to check the Eurostar website for any specific requirements or restrictions on",
      "source": "target",
