    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, what do you mean by gobstones? And what do you mean a \"goblin horde\" in the queues? I'm just asking about train travel, I don't get the references.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Gobstones, I was just using a bit of a metaphor, you see. It's a game where players move stones around on a board, trying to capture each other's stones. But I was thinking of it in a more...unconventional way. You know, like how a pack of gobstones can multiply and become overwhelming, just like a group of goblins can seem to appear out of nowhere and overwhelm a traveler. (laughs) Sorry, I know it's a bit of a stretch!\n\nAnd the \"goblin horde\" in the queues, well, it's just a playful way of describing the crowds of people that can form at train stations. You know, like a horde of goblins, swarming and pressing in on each other, trying to get to their destination. (chuckles) But I assure you, it's just a figure of speech, and not meant to be taken literally.\n\nNow, back to your train travel... (smiling)",
